// Title: Service Registry Key Deleted Via Reg.EXE
// Sigma ID: 05b2aa93-1210-42c8-8d9a-2fcc13b284f5
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-08-01 | Modified: 2023-02-04
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects execution of "reg.exe" commands with the "delete" flag on services registry key. Often
//   used by attacker to remove AV software services
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/2bcd5702a7565952c44075ac6fb946c7780526640d1264f692c7664c02c68465
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_reg_delete_services.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "reg.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "reg.exe") and ProcessCommandLine contains " delete " and ProcessCommandLine contains "\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\services\\"
